3 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671323 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671323 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\left(4-5y^{2}\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y$." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671323 1072 #uuid "100f3bc0-faf0-5120-ae97-28d49f237446" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671323 1074 "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $\\int y^p\\,\\mathrm{d}y=y^{p+1}/(p+1)+C$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\left(4-5y^{2}\\right)^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-40y^{2}+16+25y^{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -40\\int y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y+16\\int y^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}y+25\\int y^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -40\\left(\\frac{y^{3}}{3}\\right)+16\\left(\\frac{y^{1}}{1}\\right)+25\\left(\\frac{y^{5}}{5}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{40y^{3}}{3}+16y+5y^{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671324 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671312 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671324 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671324 1071 "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int \\frac{-4t^{2}+6}{t^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $t\\ne0$." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671324 1072 #uuid "15374ade-be7d-56c6-9f1a-1fc3902b8289" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671324 1074 "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $\\int t^p\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{p+1}/(p+1)+C$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{-4t^{2}+6}{t^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-4+\\frac{6}{t^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -4\\int t^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+6\\int t^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -4\\left(\\frac{t^{1}}{1}\\right)+6\\left(\\frac{t^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -4t-\\frac{6}{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true]