nstant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671339 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671294 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671339 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671339 1071 "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int -\\sqrt[4]{y}-y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $y>0$." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671339 1072 #uuid "9bd10796-f3b1-5e70-8aec-1213f51f7042" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671339 1074 "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $\\int y^p\\,\\mathrm{d}y=y^{p+1}/(p+1)+C$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int -\\sqrt[4]{y}-y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-y^{\\frac{1}{4}}-y^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -\\int y^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y-\\int y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -\\left(\\frac{y^{\\frac{5}{4}}}{\\frac{5}{4}}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{y^{3}}{3}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{4\\sqrt[4]{y^{5}}}{5}-\\frac{y^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671340 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671314 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671340 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671340 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int 2t^{3}+3t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671340 1072 #uuid "ad230c5a-f6ae-5e42-b9ee-1270504fcba4" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671340 1074 "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $\\int t^p\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{p+1}/(p+1)+C$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int 2t^{3}+3t\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(2t^{3}+3t\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= 2\\int t^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+3\\int t^{1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= 2\\left(\\frac{t^{4}}{4}\\right)+3\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{t^{4}}{2}+\\frac{3t^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671341 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671309 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671341 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671341 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int 1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$. Assume $x>0$." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671341 1072 #uuid "b1e8086a-2c48-594b-92ec-d3a3283ff1e1" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671341 1074 "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $\\int x^p\\,\\mathrm{d}x=x^{p+1}/(p+1)+C$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int 1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(1+\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int x^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{x^{1}}{1}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}}{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)+C\\\\ &= x-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671342 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671290 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671342 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671342 1071 "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$\\displaystyle\\int t^{6}-2\\,\\mathrm{d}t=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$." 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671342 1072 #uuid "cd03c39d-36ff-57e6-8cc7-8339f387c296" 13194139538659 17592186576411 true] [17592186671342 1074 "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $\\int t^p\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{p+1}/(p+1)+C$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int t^{6}-2\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(t^{6}-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int t^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-2\\int t^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{t^{7}}{7}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{t^{1}}{1}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{t^{7}}{7}-2t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank." 13194139538659 